  "findings": [
    "Canonical H remains 1.0.1-research, RESEARCH_ONLY, execution disabled, PUT 2\u20135 DTE with no roll action. Proposal dot-h-dte3-5-v1 narrows to 3\u20135 and retains exact baseline/risk/cost/execution refs.",
    "proposal-consumer.ts extracts existing qualification into qualifyDotProposal. H/D generator dispatch, eligibleFamilies routing gate, PIT feature requirements, research receipt and exit-comparison behavior are unchanged.",
    "Contracts forbid changed riskLimitVersion, multiplierSemantics, costModelVersion and executionModelVersion; require identical hard-rule sets and forbid expanded allowedActions. Shared qualification also blocks any changed allowedActions, model/policy/feature/lattice-version refs, optionType, delta buckets or DTE expansion.",
    "plannedHoldingDays and profitTakingChallengers remain unconsumed entry-consumer fields. Existing exit-comparison uses plannedHoldingDays as maxHoldingMinutes and retains all policy trials; no new selected-winner-only economic authority.",
    "H lifecycle/frontier remain byte-identical: no roll; mandatory-close triggers include event, AEGIS or liquidity deterioration and DTE<=1; closed-market expiry assignment/expiry reconciliation preserved; infeasible mandatory action recorded explicitly. This is code compatibility, not a claim all runtime close actions occur.",
    "New 34b630e management-input-state change canonicalizes valid pg Date timestamps to ISO, invalid Date to null. It can change runtime evidence qualification and input hashes for formerly locale-stringified dates; existing synthetic results do not establish current live evidence quality.",
    "34b630e also preserves allowlisted failed provider error codes/database precedence, includes POSTGRES_EAI_AGAIN in existing recovery circuit, and renders sizing reason codes/details without changing quantity."
